Each participation write adds `AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blocked_accounts k WHERE k.github_id = ?)` inside its own single statement:
- comments postSQL;
- votes Cast's INSERT…SELECT;
- votes Withdraw's DELETE;
- feedback sendSQL.

When 0 rows are written, a follow-up read in the same package (`SELECT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blocked_accounts WHERE github_id = ?)`) picks the error:
- blocked: ErrBlocked (comments.ErrBlocked; feedback.ErrBlocked = comments.ErrBlocked, as ErrBadBody already is; votes.ErrBlocked of its own);
- otherwise: the existing answer (ErrNoTarget, ErrNotOpen, or nil for a no-op Withdraw).

The write was already refused atomically; the read only chooses the wording. postComment, vote and postFeedback map ErrBlocked to 403 'Your account cannot take part here.' and store nothing. Public and OwnerTally are unchanged, so the account's existing vote keeps counting. landing()'s comment about a blocked post being 'stored, never drawn' is rewritten.

New adminRoutes rows:
- POST /admin/users/{u}/block:
  - canonicalID fails: 404;
  - auth.IsOwner(a.cfg.OwnerGitHubID, u): 400 'The author cannot be blocked.';
  - Block error: 500;
  - otherwise: 303 to /admin/blocked#blocked-<u>.
- POST /admin/users/{u}/unblock: canonicalID fails: 404; Unblock error: 500; otherwise 303 to /admin/blocked.
- GET /admin/blocked: Blocked(ctx), then OwnerInboxBySender for each account. Any error gives 500, never an empty page. It renders the new templates/admin_blocked.html.

admin_blocked.html is `<main data-hband-admin>`, with one `<section class="blocked-account" id="blocked-<u>">` per account. Each section holds:
- an h2 with `<span class="login">` (or 'GitHub user <u>' when there is no users row);
- an Unblock form posting to /admin/users/<u>/unblock;
- a `<ul>` with one `<li>` per comment: its body (or 'removed' with no text), ' on <a href="/reports/<slug>">Title</a>', and for a reply `<a href="/reports/<slug>#comment-<parent>">the one it answered</a>`;
- a `<ul>` of its feedback, each item with its body and report link.

admin.html gains a 'Blocked users' link. The moderation list gains `<details class="block"><summary>Block</summary><form … action="/admin/users/<GitHubID>/block"><button>Block @login</button></form></details>` on items not written by the owner.

contracts.error_cases:
From the gate:
- identify failure: 503;
- anonymous POST: 403;
- signed-in non-owner, including one with the owner's login and another id: a 403 forbidden page;
- cross-site: 403;
- GET or HEAD: 405 from the mux.

From the handler:
- n not canonical, unknown, or the comment was deleted with its report: 404;
- an unreadable body or one over 1 KiB: 400;
- `from` present with a value other than exactly 'admin', or repeated: 400;
- a store error: 500.

Every refusal changes nothing.

